      "comment": "LAKE PICHOLA (9) took charge early on and kept going to record an emphatic 7 metres win last start over 2100m at this track, following on from his success when resuming at Narrogin. His last-start form is good enough to win a race of this calibre. CONTROL THE ROOM (6) was prominent from the outset last time out and was runner-up, beaten a head, in a far better performance at Gloucester Park over 2130m. Finds a nice race and will prove very tough to beat once more. CIGANDA (7) didn't do a bad job when fourth over 2185m at Pinjarra last time out. Each-way claims. VISITING HOURS (1) has drawn to advantage and should give backers a great sight.",
